YAAP: 61-cdi-val-hum-fem-neu ... just for kicks!
****
After finishing the stylish samurai, I had planned on trying a unihorn
wielding tourist.  That turned to custard c/o a Minotaur just below
minetown.  Shortly after that on IRC I said something along the lines
of, "No more screwing around."  This game was personal.  I decided on
a long sword + short sword valkyrie.  Mostly, I was curious how
noticeable the difference in melee offense [1] would be.

Despite the lighter offense, this game was actually easier.

>From T:1, I had absolutely no doubt I would ascend.  The RNG tried to
outfox me.  Early on, I was down to HP:1(16) with a fox adjacent while
trying (and failing) to Elbereth.  I survived.

I think the RNG conceded defeat, because damn near everything went my
way from then on.

A very early magic lamp wish netted the blessed greased +2 grey dragon
scale mail I wore to the end.  Sokoban was the reflection variant.
Before reaching minetown, I had at least one wand of death (probably
two, but memory is hazy on that).

There were only a few memorably tense moments.

Just below minetown, I encountered the same minotaur that killed my
previous tourist, along with a rogue named thirteen.  One /death
charge later and the minotaur (along with my tourist's warhorse,
Purchased for a Kingdom) were nice and dead.  I got my stuff back!

During my visit to Vlad's, a Titan greated me with summon nasties.  As
soon as that mess was cleaned up, an Archon spawned two/three step
behind me.  It took two rounds kill it in melee (and it didn't get to
attack either).  This archon dropped Demonbane, and I could have
completed the set, Sunsword was lying on the ground on the plane of
Earth.

During the ascension run, I stupidly moved next to a purple h in
Asmodeus' lair.  I got flayed.  Fortunately, my ascension kit is
standardized and compact enough that (re)identifying my gear was a
trivial exercise.  The missing maps made the ascension run take longer
than I prefer, but I managed.

Astral was just your typical three-Altar tour.  The last altar was
guarded by Death (as always).  I killed him in a doorway.
Unfortunately, some tough hostiles reached the door before me.
Teleporting them away was not viable ... so ... I had to suck it up
and melee.  The "light" offense I went with meant it took (at most)
one extra turn to kill an angel.

This is my fastest ascension yet (28,631 turns) despite lollygagging
about once I had the amulet (2,479 turns) and taking the scenic route
in the planes (270 turns, 111 on astral).

The full endgame dump can be found at:
http://alt.org/nethack/chardump/cdi/cdi.20070424-003001.txt

-cdi

[1] 34.0/37.0 for the valkyrie, compared to 37.0/39.0 for the samurai
